w("Everything below is produced by `scripts/p2_01..p2_05` (outputs in `data/processed/phase2/`); this file is generated by `scripts/p2_05_write_notes.py`, so every measured number is read from a saved result. Reusable code: `src/features/groups.py`, `src/features/stability_data.py`, `src/models/stages.py`, `src/eval/metrics.py`, `src/conformal/recall.py`, with tests in `tests/`.")
w("")
w("## 0. Design choices and caveats (read first)")
w("")
w("- **Groups are proxies.** The released data has no MOFid (see `notes/stability_inventory.md`), so groups are connected components over *4-letter CSD refcode family* and *DOI* (DOIs exist only for the 2,179 solvent-table MOFs). MOFs that are the same material under different refcodes and without a shared DOI can still end up in different groups, so some leakage may remain.")
w("- **One split for all three tasks.** Groups are built on the union of the three tables (4,963 MOFs) and each group is assigned once to train / calibration / test (60/20/20 by MOF count, seed 0), so a MOF has the same role in every task.")
w("- **Smaller training sets than the paper.** 60% of MOFs train each model (the released scripts use 80%); 20% is held out for calibration and 20% for test. The 'random' comparison uses the same 60/20/20 sizes and the same code, with MOF-level random assignment, so the two columns differ only in how MOFs are assigned.")
w("- **Features come from each task's own CSV** (not the merged `all_in_one` table whose substitutions the audit found), using the released feature columns (170 / 170 / 159).")
w("- **Honest training:** the early-stopping restore is fixed (`copy.deepcopy` of the best state; unit-tested to return exactly the best-epoch weights). The 10% validation set used for early stopping is also held out by group. Released architectures and hyperparameters are used unchanged (thermal and solvent networks, 5 seeds); the water forest uses the released best parameters (200 trees, no depth limit, bootstrap off) and was **not re-tuned** with group-aware cross-validation.")
w("- **'Stable' is defined as in the paper's screening (SI Section 4):** thermal decomposition temperature >= 350 degC; solvent label +1; water class 2 or 3 (0-based). Stage scores for conformal control: thermal = predicted temperature, solvent = predicted probability, water = P(class 2) + P(class 3).")
w("")
w("## 1. Group-aware splits")
w("")
w(f"{gs['n_mofs']:,} MOFs (union of the three tables) form **{gs['n_groups']:,} groups**. Every group lies wholly in one split (checked in `p2_01_groups.py` by assertion).")
w("")
w("| group size (MOFs) | groups | MOFs |")
w("|---|---|---|")
for r in gs["sizes"]:
    w(f"| {r['size']} | {r['groups']:,} | {r['mofs']:,} |")
sz = groups.drop_duplicates("group_id")["group_size"]
w("")
w(f"Largest groups: {', '.join(str(x) for x in sorted(sz.tolist(), reverse=True)[:8])}; median group size {int(sz.median())}, mean {sz.mean():.2f}. No giant component: the largest group is {sz.max()} MOFs ({pc(sz.max() / gs['n_mofs'])} of all).")
w("")
w("| split | groups | MOFs | fraction | largest group |")
w("|---|---|---|---|---|")
for r in gs["per_split"]:
    w(f"| {r['split']} | {r['groups']:,} | {r['mofs']:,} | {pc(r['frac'])} | {r['largest_group']} |")
w("")
w("| task | MOFs | train | calibration | test | stable in train / cal / test |")
